# Python Programming Lab Applications

This repository contains the implementations of Python Programming Lab experiments based on Object-Oriented Programming, Functional Programming, Generators, Iterators, Decorators, Multithreading, Multiprocessing, Asynchronous Programming, Exception Handling, Logging, and Memory Profiling.

Each experiment is implemented in a separate Jupyter Notebook.

---

## Experiments

| File         | Experiment                                             | Main Concepts                                                  |
| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `APP1.ipynb` | Zomato-like Food Delivery Management System            | Classes, Objects, Inheritance, OOP                             |
| `APP2.ipynb` | SBI YONO Digital Banking System                        | Encapsulation, Inheritance, Polymorphism, Operator Overloading |
| `APP3.ipynb` | Zoomcar Vehicle Rental Management System               | Class Hierarchy, Inheritance, Special Methods                  |
| `APP4.ipynb` | Amazon Customer Purchase Analytics                     | Lambda, Map, Filter, Reduce                                    |
| `APP5.ipynb` | BESCOM Smart Electricity Consumption Monitoring System | Generators, Iterators, `yield`                                 |
| `APP6.ipynb` | Google Fit Inspired Activity Monitoring System         | Decorators, Closures, Higher-Order Functions                   |
| `APP7.ipynb` | IDM-like Multi-File Download Manager                   | Multithreading, Thread Synchronization                         |
| `APP8.ipynb` | Zoho Payroll Processing System                         | Multiprocessing, AsyncIO, Asynchronous Programming             |
| `APP9.ipynb` | NPTEL Online Examination System                        | Exception Handling, Logging, Assertions, Memory Profiling      |

---

# Detailed Experiments

## APP1 – Zomato-like Food Delivery Management System

A food delivery management system designed using Python classes and inheritance.

### Concepts Used

* Classes and Objects
* Constructors
* Inheritance
* Object-Oriented Programming

### Main Classes

`User`, `Customer`, `PremiumCustomer`, `DeliveryPartner`, `Restaurant`, `Order`

### Main Methods

`place_order()`, `calculate_discount()`, `assign_delivery()`, `generate_bill()`, `display_details()`

---

## APP2 – SBI YONO Digital Banking System

A digital banking system demonstrating encapsulation, polymorphism, and operator overloading.

### Concepts Used

* Encapsulation
* Inheritance
* Runtime Polymorphism
* Operator Overloading
* Private Attributes

### Main Classes

`BankAccount`, `SavingsAccount`, `CurrentAccount`, `FixedDepositAccount`

### Special Methods

* `__add__()`
* `__gt__()`

### Main Operations

* Deposit
* Withdraw
* Interest calculation
* Balance management
* PIN management

---

## APP3 – Zoomcar Vehicle Rental Management System

A vehicle rental management system using class hierarchies and Python special methods.

### Concepts Used

* Class Hierarchy
* Inheritance
* Python Special Methods
* Object Creation and Deletion

### Main Classes

`Vehicle`, `Car`, `Bike`, `ElectricScooter`, `Rental`

### Special Methods

* `__init__()`
* `__str__()`
* `__repr__()`
* `__len__()`
* `__del__()`

### Main Operations

* Vehicle management
* Rental management
* Rental charge calculation
* Vehicle category handling

---

## APP4 – Amazon Customer Purchase Analytics

A customer purchase analytics system for processing purchase records using functional programming.

### Concepts Used

* Lambda Functions
* `map()`
* `filter()`
* `reduce()`
* Functional Programming

### Main Operations

* Calculate purchase totals
* Transform purchase records
* Filter high-value purchases
* Calculate total sales
* Calculate average purchase value
* Identify high-value purchases

---

## APP5 – BESCOM Smart Electricity Consumption Monitoring System

An electricity consumption monitoring system that processes readings sequentially using generators and iterators.

### Concepts Used

* Generators
* Iterators
* `yield`
* `__iter__()`
* `__next__()`

### Main Operations

* Generate electricity readings
* Process readings sequentially
* Calculate total consumption
* Calculate average consumption
* Identify high-consumption readings
* Monitor electricity usage

---

## APP6 – Google Fit Inspired Activity Monitoring System

An activity monitoring system using decorators, closures, and higher-order functions.

### Concepts Used

* Decorators
* Closures
* Higher-Order Functions
* Function Authentication
* Execution-Time Monitoring

### Main Decorators

* `authenticate()`
* `log_execution()`
* `execution_timer()`

### Main Operations

* Authenticate users
* Log activity execution
* Calculate execution time
* Apply multiple decorators
* Monitor activity records

---

## APP7 – IDM-like Multi-File Download Manager

A multi-file download manager designed to demonstrate concurrent execution using Python multithreading.

### Concepts Used

* Multithreading
* Thread Synchronization
* Concurrent Execution
* `start()`
* `join()`

### Main Class

`DownloadThread`

### Main Methods

* `run()`
* `start()`
* `join()`

### Main Operations

* Create multiple download threads
* Process multiple files concurrently
* Synchronize thread execution
* Display download status
* Wait for thread completion

---

## APP8 – Zoho Payroll Processing System

A payroll processing system demonstrating multiprocessing and asynchronous programming.

### Concepts Used

* Multiprocessing
* AsyncIO
* Asynchronous Programming
* `async`
* `await`
* `gather()`

### Main Classes

`Employee`, `PayrollProcessor`

### Main Methods / Functions

* `Process()`
* `Pool()`
* `async`
* `await`
* `gather()`

### Main Operations

* Create employee payroll records
* Calculate salaries
* Process CPU-intensive payroll tasks
* Retrieve employee information asynchronously
* Perform concurrent asynchronous operations
* Generate payroll reports

---

## APP9 – NPTEL Online Examination System

An online examination system demonstrating exception handling, logging, assertions, and memory profiling.

### Concepts Used

* Exception Handling
* Logging
* Assertions
* Memory Profiling
* `tracemalloc`

### Main Classes

`Exam`, `Student`, `Question`

### Main Logging Functions

* `logging.info()`
* `logging.error()`

### Main Operations

* Create examination questions
* Accept student details and answers
* Validate user inputs
* Handle invalid inputs
* Log important events and errors
* Monitor memory usage
* Calculate examination score
* Display examination results

